<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Video library (SPEC 5/6, Builder B). Mockups: Movies.dc (500), MoviesPoster.dc (501), TV.dc (502).
	Includes: Includes_Views_Video.xml (VidView_*), View_50_List from Includes_Views.xml.

	Kodi id contract (Estuary Omega MyVideoNav.xml + CGUIWindowVideoNav, Omega source):
	  1.0.18: <views> reordered 502,500,503,501,50,506,507 (every view is typed "list", so a node's default is the FIRST
	  visible one; saved views match by id + type, so the order changes no saved view). With the widened views this
	  keeps every default: movies / sets 500, tvshows / seasons 502, episodes 503, genres / years / people / files 50.
	  507 Stills (wide grid) is new and last. Before 1.0.18:
	  <views> containers 500/501/502/503/50 + 506 Poster wall appended LAST (Includes_Wall.xml, generated) (first visible one is the default for a new node, so
	  movies/sets open in 500, tvshows/seasons in 502, episodes in 503, everything else in 50);
	  menucontrol 9000 (header filter bar); 3 sort-by / 4 sort-order (hidden buttons the bar clicks);
	  14 watched toggle (SendClick only, no control needed); defaultcontrol 50 = Kodi focuses the
	  active view. Majan ids: 9310 Next up strip, 9321-9326 header buttons, 63 scrollbar of 503.

	Focus map: header 9000 ↓ Next up 9310 (TV root, when it has items) ↓ view. View ↑ (top row)
	→ Next up or header. Back = Kodi parent folder; Back on the header returns to the view.
-->
<window>
	<defaultcontrol always="true">50</defaultcontrol>
	<menucontrol>9000</menucontrol>
	<backgroundcolor>bg</backgroundcolor>
	<views>502,500,503,501,50,506,507</views>
	<onload condition="$EXP[ArtBackgroundOn]">SetProperty(TMDbHelper.Blur.SourceImage,Art(fanart)|Art(tvshow.fanart)|Art(poster)|Art(tvshow.poster)|Art(thumb),Home)</onload>
	<!-- new stamp each time this window opens, as Home does: the Next up plugin path changes, so a plug-in row refreshes after playback -->
	<onload condition="System.AddonIsEnabled(script.embuary.helper)">SetProperty(majan.reload,$INFO[System.Time(hh:mm:ss)],home)</onload>
	<!-- empty folder: Kodi can't focus an empty view, so land on the header bar instead -->
	<onload condition="Integer.IsEqual(Container.NumItems,0) + !Container.IsUpdating">SetFocus(9000)</onload>
	<include>Anim_WindowOpenClose</include>
	<controls>
		<include>VidView_Window</include>
	</controls>
</window>
